Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: restart AN through Clause 45-only MDIO bridges

The PHY package bitmap describes the PHY, not the bridge. A device may
advertise Clause 22 registers while its MDIO bridge provides only Clause
45 callbacks, as with MDIO_I2C_ROLLBALL. Choosing Clause 22 in that case
makes an otherwise supported AN restart return -EOPNOTSUPP.

Keep the existing selection for Clause 22 PHYs, dual-protocol buses, and
Clause 45 PHYs without an AN MMD or without both required bus callbacks.
For a Clause 45-only transport with an AN MMD, use the normal Clause 45
restart helper. No advertisement or PHY firmware settings are changed.
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/phy.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/phy.c
@@ -182,7 +182,15 @@
 {
 	int ret;
 
-	if (phydev->is_c45 && !(phydev->c45_ids.devices_in_package & BIT(0)))
+	/* A Clause 45 PHY can also advertise Clause 22 registers, but an
+	 * MDIO bridge may only transport Clause 45 transactions. Use the
+	 * available AN MMD instead of issuing unsupported Clause 22 I/O.
+	 */
+	if (phydev->is_c45 &&
+	    (!(phydev->c45_ids.devices_in_package & BIT(0)) ||
+	     ((!phydev->mdio.bus->read || !phydev->mdio.bus->write) &&
+	      phydev->mdio.bus->read_c45 && phydev->mdio.bus->write_c45 &&
+	      (phydev->c45_ids.mmds_present & MDIO_DEVS_AN))))
 		ret = genphy_c45_restart_aneg(phydev);
 	else
 		ret = genphy_restart_aneg(phydev);
